SuberTube Deployment Runbook & Release Sign-Off Gate
Document Version: 1.0.0
Initial Approval Status: CONDITIONAL
Target: SuberTube Release APK (app-release.apk)

1. Overview & Gate Preconditions
This runbook defines the mandatory verification procedure required to transition SuberTube from CONDITIONAL to fully APPROVED deployment status. No distribution or installation on production devices may take place until all four execution stages are completed and signed off.

Gate Status Definitions
CONDITIONAL (Current Baseline): Source code, static regression tests, security preflights, and local asset isolation verified. Binary APK compilation, standalone checksum validation, and antivirus scanning pending.
APPROVED: All checksums match, Malwarebytes scan returns zero threats, and technical leads have verified runtime integrity.
BLOCKED: Any checksum mismatch, unauthorized secret exposure, foreign script injection, or malicious/suspicious malware verdict.
2. Stage 1 — Build APK via GitHub Actions
2.1 Preflight Configuration Check
Ensure the repository contains the release workflow and required GitHub Secrets:

Workflow path: .github/workflows/build-release-apk.yml
Repository Secrets (Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions):
KEYSTORE_PATH: relative path or filename (e.g. keystore.jks)
KEYSTORE_PASSWORD: keystore store password
KEY_ALIAS: release key alias
KEY_PASSWORD: private key password
2.2 Execution
Navigate to the repository on GitHub.
Open the Actions tab.
Select Android Release Build from the workflow sidebar.
Click Run workflow -> select branch main -> click Run workflow.
2.3 Verification & Artifact Collection
Confirm all steps pass successfully:
Node Quality Gate (npm test)
Security Preflight (npm run security)
Release Integrity (npm run integrity)
Release Build (./gradlew :app:assembleRelease)
In the completed workflow run summary, scroll to Artifacts.
Download the artifact bundle app-release (contains app-release.apk and RELEASE-SHA256SUMS.txt).
Extract the artifact into a dedicated staging directory:
mkdir -p ./release-staging
unzip app-release.zip -d ./release-staging
3. Stage 2 — SHA256 Checksum Validation
3.1 Calculate Binary Hash
Run the standard SHA256 calculation against the compiled APK:

cd ./release-staging
sha256sum app-release.apk > APK-SHA256SUM.txt
cat APK-SHA256SUM.txt
3.2 Integrity Comparison & Evidence Logging
Record the generated hash string into the release audit ledger.
Validate that the APK was built from the signed release configuration and not a debug build:
File size expectation: compressed release bundle typically between 2MB - 10MB.
Header inspection verifies zip archive alignment and Android manifest compilation.
4. Stage 3 — Malwarebytes Antivirus & Threat Scanning
4.1 File Scanning
Submit app-release.apk to Malwarebytes Endpoint Protection / Malwarebytes Mobile Scanner.
In addition, submit the APK SHA256 hash or binary file to an authorized multi-engine analysis portal if mandated by internal security policy.
4.2 Acceptance Criteria
Evaluation Metric	Permissible Value	Action on Breach
Malwarebytes Detection Result	0 Detections / Clean	Immediate BLOCKED
Risk Score / Threat Assessment	0 / Safe	Immediate BLOCKED
Suspicious PUP / Adware Triggers	None	Review Android WebView & Origin Rules
Outbound Network Endpoints	Only *.youtube.com and local asset origin	Flag unexpected endpoints
